    {
      "kind": "theorem",
      "reading_layout": "progressive",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.RealMatrixPositiveIntegral.integral_posSemidef",
      "title": "Probability expectations preserve full real matrix positivity",
      "reader_note": "Open assumptions and source-ordered proof steps for the full conditions and adjacent exact Lean.",
      "statement": "An integrable, almost-everywhere positive semidefinite real matrix map has a positive semidefinite probability expectation.",
      "formula": "f\\in L^1(\\mu),\\quad f(\\omega)\\succeq0\\ \\mu\\text{-a.e.}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\int f\\,d\\mu\\succeq0.",
      "assumptions": [
        "Let \\(n\\) be a finite index set, possibly empty, and let \\((\\Omega,\\mu)\\) be any measurable probability space. The function \\(f\\) takes values in real \\(n\\)-by-\\(n\\) matrices.",
        "The explicit authored contracts are \\(f\\in L^1(\\mu)\\) and \\(f(\\omega)\\succeq0\\) almost everywhere. Integrability includes an a.e. strongly measurable representative and finite extended-norm integral.",
        "Here \\(A\\succeq0\\) means both \\(A^\\top=A\\) and \\(v^\\top A v\\ge0\\) for every finite vector. Positivity is full matrix PSD, rather than entrywise positivity.",
        "The matrix space uses its complete Euclidean operator norm and the integral is Bochner. No caller-supplied closed/convex cone, pointwise measurability, nonempty matrix index or representative certificate is required.",
        "This arbitrary-function background statement is authored explicitly. Concrete Gaussian consumers prove its contracts internally; the original Gaussian Source Anchor gains no new premise."
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Fix the full PSD cone and the actual integral contract",
          "text": "Use the literal finite real matrix space and the genuine integrable, a.e. PSD function. The full signature permits empty finite indices. Its standard operator-norm and completeness instances are synthesized internally.",
          "formula": "\\mathcal P=\\{A:A^\\top=A,\\ v^\\top A v\\ge0\\ \\text{for every }v\\}.",
          "lean": "import Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Star.Real\nimport Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Integral\nimport Mathlib.Analysis.CStarAlgebra.Matrix\nimport Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.PosDef\n\n/-! ASTIS-authored reusable background for positivity under expectation.\nThe full PSD cone geometry is proved here once. Concrete source applications\nmust derive integrability and AE positivity internally. Empty finite matrix\nindices are permitted. This is not a printed generic theorem in the paper. -/\n\nnoncomputable section\nopen MeasureTheory\nopen scoped Matrix.Norms.L2Operator\nset_option autoImplicit false\n\nnamespace AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.RealMatrixPositiveIntegral\n\ntheorem integral_posSemidef\n    {n Ω : Type*} [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n] [MeasurableSpace Ω]\n    {μ : Measure Ω} [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]\n    (f : Ω → Matrix n n ℝ) (hf : Integrable f μ)\n    (hpos : ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, Matrix.PosSemidef (f ω)) :\n    Matrix.PosSemidef (∫ ω, f ω ∂μ)\n:= by\n  classical\n  let M := Matrix n n ℝ\n"
        },
        {
          "title": "Prove the cone closed in the declared topology",
          "text": "Hermitian matrices form the equalizer of continuous star and identity. For every fixed finite vector, its quadratic evaluation is continuous and the nonnegative half-line is closed. Intersect these closed conditions; no cone-geometry certificate is a public input.",
          "formula": "\\mathcal P=\\{A:A^\\top=A\\}\\cap\\bigcap_v\\{A:v^\\top A v\\ge0\\}.",
          "lean": "  have PSD_closed : IsClosed {A : M | A.PosSemidef} := by\n    have hermitian_closed : IsClosed {A : M | A.IsHermitian} := by\n      change IsClosed {A : M | star A = A}\n      exact isClosed_eq continuous_star continuous_id\n    have quadratic_closed (v : n → ℝ) :\n        IsClosed {A : M | 0 ≤ dotProduct (star v) (Matrix.mulVec A v)} := by\n      apply isClosed_le continuous_const\n      change Continuous (fun A : M => ∑ a, star (v a) * ∑ b, A a b * v b)\n      fun_prop\n    convert hermitian_closed.inter (isClosed_iInter quadratic_closed) using 1\n    ext A\n    simp [Matrix.posSemidef_iff_dotProduct_mulVec]\n"
        },
        {
          "title": "Use convexity and the canonical probability integral theorem",
          "text": "Nonnegative scalar combinations of full PSD matrices remain PSD, proving convexity. Apply the existing closed-convex integral theorem to the actual a.e. membership and integrability hypotheses. The proof does not strengthen a.e. positivity to pointwise positivity.",
          "formula": "a,b\\ge0,\\ a+b=1,\\ A,B\\in\\mathcal P\\Longrightarrow aA+bB\\in\\mathcal P,\\qquad\\int f\\,d\\mu\\in\\mathcal P.",
          "lean": "  have PSD_convex : Convex ℝ {A : M | A.PosSemidef} := by\n    intro A hA B hB a b ha hb hab\n    exact (hA.smul ha).add (hB.smul hb)\n  exact PSD_convex.integral_mem PSD_closed hpos hf\n\nend AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.RealMatrixPositiveIntegral\n"
        }
      ],
